    "rationale": "The histopathologic findings of atypical lymphocytes, a CD4-predominant infiltrate with loss of CD8, and monoclonal T-cell gene rearrangement are diagnostic of mycosis fungoides, a specific cutaneous T-cell lymphoma. Follicular mucin deposition is a secondary feature often seen in folliculotropic mycosis fungoides. R3 (Cutaneous T-cell lymphoma) is a broader category, while R2 (Follicular mucinosis) lacks the atypical and clonal features.",
